# geo.js – project overview

**Goal:** A mathematics-based 3D engine (plus 2D shapes) in TypeScript that renders
the same scene equally to **Canvas 2D** and **SVG**, shipped as an npm package
(`@janwalenda/geo`) and as a minified browser bundle.

## Architecture (layers, dependencies only point downwards)

```
src/math/       Vec2, Vec3, Vec4, Mat3, Mat4, Quat, utils     – pure, no DOM
src/scene/      Object3D, Scene, Mesh, Polyline, Points,        – pure, no DOM
                Camera (Perspective/Orthographic), Lights, Material, Color
src/geometry/   Geometry + generators (Box, Plane, UVSphere,    – pure, no DOM
                Tetra/Octa/Icosahedron, Torus, Cylinder, Cone,
                Parametric)
src/shapes/     2D shapes (Shape2D: Circle, Rect, Ellipse,      – pure, no DOM
                Polygon, Line, FunctionGraph, ParametricCurve, …)
src/render/     compile(): scene + camera → DisplayList          – pure, no DOM
                (transform → near clipping → projection → culling
                 → flat shading → depth sorting)
src/renderers/  CanvasRenderer, SVGRenderer, toSVGString,        – the only place with DOM
                animate()
src/index.ts    public API (everything exported is API)
```

Core idea: geometry **never draws itself**. The pipeline produces a
renderer-neutral **DisplayList** of 2D primitives (`polygon`, `polyline`,
`circle`, `image`) with fully resolved styles; renderers only translate this list.
A new renderer therefore only needs `draw(list)`.

## Commands

| Command             | Purpose |
|---------------------|---------|
| `npm run dev`       | Demo (`index.html`, `demo/`) with the Vite dev server |
| `npm run typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit` (strict) |
| `npm test`          | Vitest once; `npm run test:watch` in watch mode |
| `npm run build`     | Rollup: `dist/geo.js` (ESM), `geo.cjs`, `geo.min.js`, `geo.umd.min.js`, `geo.d.ts` |
| `npm run test:dist` | Smoke test of all built entry points (after `build`) |

Other places: `demo/` (Vite demo, Canvas and SVG side by side, `?static` freezes it),
`test/` (**all** tests, structure mirrors `src/`, plus helpers, README examples and the
bundle smoke test `test/dist/verify-dist.mjs`),
`rollup.config.mjs` (library build), `CHANGELOG.md` (Keep a Changelog).

## Guard rails

- Layers below `src/renderers/` must **not** use `document`, `window`,
  Canvas or SVG APIs – they must be testable in Node.
- Canvas and SVG must produce **the same image** for the same DisplayList
  (same fill, stroke, line width, opacity, order).
- Export public API only through `src/index.ts`; note every visible change in the
  `[Unreleased]` section of `CHANGELOG.md` (in the same feature branch).
- Examples in `README.md` are executed by `test/readme.test.ts` – update both on API changes.

## Language

**Everything written in this repository is in English:** code, identifiers, comments,
JSDoc, README, CHANGELOG, CONTRIBUTING and all other docs, the agent rules in
`.cursor/rules/` and `CLAUDE.md`, commit messages, branch names, issue and PR texts.
(Agents may still answer the user in the user's language in chat.)
